      "technical_explanation": "The scanner raised a generic unsafe-regex signal without retaining the matched literals. The supplied source windows show the flagged region is the extension's scene-parsing logic: text-matching rules that look for motion counts, duration cues, pause cues, action vocabulary, and participant-zone references in roleplay text, which matches the project's stated purpose of converting scene text into tactile playback plans. The visible patterns use mutually exclusive word alternations, optional groups, and small fixed-bounded gap repetitions rather than nested unbounded repetition over ambiguous subpatterns, so no catastrophic-backtracking structure is demonstrated. Inputs are the user's own chat messages, processed locally and on demand. Even a pathological input would at most slow the user's own client during playback parsing, with no credential, exfiltration, persistence, or cross-user path involved.",
